<title>USA: Visa says Latam banks can issue competing cards. [CORRECTED 23:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Visa says Latam banks can issue competing cards. [CORRECTED 23:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Visa International's Latin America and Caribbean division said Tuesday that member financial institutions in the region were not prohibited from issuing American Express Co cards or others issued by competitors.</p>
<p>Visa said American Express' market share (corrects reference to market share from Visa to American Express) in Latin America has dropped in recent years, making such a prohibition unnecessary.</p>
</text>
